      "costUsd": 0.0073805,
      "pronunciationText": "Last video ended with this question. Six equal weights on a beam balance right in the middle, at three point five. That's the expected value of one roll, but a die can never show three point five. Now a lopsided case. A vet clinic finds that a cat makes zero, one, two or three visits a year, with probabilities zero point one, zero point three, zero point four and zero point two. Where does this beam balance? What does that number mean? And how spread out are the visits?"
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-02",
      "changed": true,
      "audio": "public/audio/math-a12-s03/scene-02.wav",
      "durationInFrames": 1188,
      "worstWordGap": {
