      "successfulRequestCount": 1,
      "loggedRequestAttempts": 1,
      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 151,
      "outputTokens": 990,
      "costUsd": 0.008985499999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's what the balance point means. Picture many cats, one after another, and keep a running average of their visits. This run starts two, two, three, so the average is high at first. After ten cats it's two point one. After a thousand cats, this run has settled at about one point seven. Another run would wobble differently, but long runs settle near the same centre. So the expected value is the long-run average of X. No cat makes one point seven visits. It isn't a prediction for one cat. It's the centre the results settle around. We write it as E of X, or the Greek letter mu, and it's a measure of centre for the distribution."
    },
