      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 126,
      "outputTokens": 981,
      "costUsd": 0.008892,
      "pronunciationText": "Where does one point seven come from? For a fair die, every value has the same weight, so E of X is just the ordinary average, twenty-one over six. The cat visits aren't uniform. Imagine a thousand cats. About a hundred make no visits, three hundred make one, four hundred make two and two hundred make three. That's seventeen hundred visits, so the average is one point seven. Dividing each count by a thousand gives its probability. So the expected value is the sum of each value times its probability. And the beam balances at one point seven, pulled towards the heavier bars."
    },
