      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 133,
      "outputTokens": 1062,
      "costUsd": 0.009624500000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "Now, spread. A natural idea is to average how far each value is from mu, keeping the sign. These signed deviations are minus one point seven, minus zero point seven, zero point three and one point three. Weight each one by its probability, and add. You get exactly zero. That's not bad luck. Mu is the balance point, so the weighted deviations on the left always cancel the ones on the right. So we square each deviation first, which makes none of them negative, and then take the weighted average. That's the variance. It's an expected value too: the expected value of the squared deviation from mu."
    },
