      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 127,
      "outputTokens": 942,
      "costUsd": 0.008541499999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "Here it is for the cats. The squared deviations are two point eight nine, zero point four nine, zero point zero nine and one point six nine. Weight them and add, and the variance is zero point eight one. But squaring changed the units. X counts visits, so the variance is in visits squared. So take the square root. The standard deviation, sigma, is the square root of zero point eight one, which is zero point nine. It measures the spread, in visits. Here, the values within one sigma of one point seven, from zero point eight to two point six, carry most of the probability."
    },
