      "inputTokens": 151,
      "outputTokens": 1122,
      "costUsd": 0.010173499999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "There's a faster way to get the same number. Expand the square: x minus mu, squared, is x squared, minus two mu x, plus mu squared. Weight each part and add. The middle part has the sum of x times P of x, which is mu. The last has the sum of the probabilities, which is one. What's left is E of X squared, the average of the squared values, minus mu squared. For our distribution, E of X squared is three point seven, and three point seven minus one point seven squared is zero point eight one, the same answer. Be careful. E of X squared squares the values, not the probabilities, and it isn't the same as mu squared."
