      "pronunciationText": "Use both facts. The probabilities add to one, so a plus b is zero point eight. And the expected value gives zero point two, plus two a, plus three b, equals two point three, so two a plus three b is two point one. Take away twice the first equation, and b is zero point five, so ay is zero point three. A and b both zero point four is wrong. It uses only one fact, and its expected value is two point two."
